# .trivyignore — reviewed & accepted findings for the Trivy filesystem scan.
#
# Purpose
#   This file lists vulnerability IDs that have been triaged and consciously
#   accepted, so the Trivy fs scan can be flipped from advisory to BLOCKING
#   without unfixable base-image noise failing the gate. Every entry MUST be a
#   deliberate, reviewed decision — not a way to silence real findings.
#
# Policy
#   - Only add a CVE here after review. Prefer fixing (bump the dependency or
#     base image) over ignoring.
#   - Document WHY each entry is accepted and, where possible, an expiry so it
#     gets revisited. Trivy honors an optional trailing "exp:YYYY-MM-DD".
#   - Application-dependency CVEs should be FIXED, not ignored. This list is
#     intended for base-image OS packages with no upstream fix available.
#
# Format
#   One vulnerability ID per line (e.g. CVE-2024-XXXXX). Blank lines and
#   lines starting with "#" are ignored.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accepted: base-image OS CVEs with NO fix available
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The python:3.x-slim (Debian) and nginx:1.27-alpine base images periodically
# carry OS-package CVEs for which no fixed version has been released upstream.
# These are unfixable from our side until the distro ships a patched package
# and we rebuild; they are accepted here and reviewed on each base-image bump.
#
# (No specific unfixable CVE IDs pinned at this time — add them below as they
#  are triaged, one per line, each with a short justification comment.)
#
# Example (template — uncomment and adapt when a finding is accepted):
# CVE-2023-45853   # zlib in base image; no Debian fix; not reachable at runtime  exp:2026-12-31
